  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $g(x)=x^2+x-2$ and $\\frac{1}{2} g o f(x)=2 x^2-5 x+2$ then $f(x)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "O6wOj",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x-3$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wgoDp",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x+3$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7wcHd",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x^2+3 x+1$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19gRS",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x^2-3 x+1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $\\frac{1}{2} go f(x)=2 x^2-5 x+2$\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n& \\Rightarrow g(f(x))=4 x^2-10 x+4 \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow(f(x))^2+f(x)-2=4 x^2-10 x+4 \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow(f(x))^2+f(x)-\\left(4 x^2-10 x+6\\right)=0 \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1+4\\left(4 x^2-10 x+6\\right)}}{2} \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{16 x^2-40 x+25}}{2} \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow f(x)=\\frac{-1 \\pm(4 x-5)}{2}=2 x-3,-2 x+2\r\n\\end{aligned}$\r\nHence, $f(x)=2 x-3$",
    "image": null
  },
